+# Ticket #4471: no session replays for the new UI
+
+## Why
+
+Session replay on mobile is driven by the `PostHogWidget` wrapper. `posthog_flutter`
+captures screenshots from the subtree under that widget and sends them to the native
+SDK. Its docs say the app must be wrapped in `PostHogWidget` when
+`PostHogConfig.sessionReplay` is on (`lib/src/posthog_widget.dart` in
+posthog_flutter 5.55.0; the 5.36.3 copy has the same doc comment).
+
+- `lib/legacy_app.dart` wraps `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. Replays work for the A/B group.
+- `lib/new_app.dart` returned `MaterialApp.router` with no wrapper. Replay was enabled
+  (`lib/analytics.dart`: `sessionReplay = true`) but there was no widget tree to capture.
+
+Events still arrive for the new UI because the SDK is set up in `main.dart` and
+`PosthogObserver` is attached to the GoRouter, so screen events and custom events
+(`loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`) are unaffected. That matches the ticket.
+
+## Fix
+
+`lib/new_app.dart`: wrap `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`, the same as `LegacyApp`.
+No other changes. The `posthog_flutter` import was already present.
+
+## Not verified
+
+- I did not run the app or check a recording in PostHog. `flutter analyze` could not run
+  because the package config is not resolved in this checkout. I ran `dart format` on the
+  file, which parses it.
+- The `phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI` project key in `lib/analytics.dart` is a CI placeholder and was left unchanged.
+- Confirm on a new-UI device build after the change that a recording appears in the Replay tab.
